# Implementation Plan: GPS & Mobile Attendance Channel (Production Engine)

Convert the **GPS & Mobile Attendance Channel** into a fully production-grade, authoritative attendance channel connecting **HR Web Portal**, **Supabase PostgreSQL & Realtime**, and **Flutter Mobile App**. All operations will use real database tables and real device GPS without any simulation or hardcoded mock coordinates.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Real Device GPS**: The Flutter mobile app will use the `geolocator` package to acquire live device GPS (`latitude`, `longitude`, `accuracy`). If location permissions are denied or GPS is turned off, clear actionable prompts will guide the user to system settings.
> - **Server-Authoritative Validation**: The client device sends GPS coordinates to Supabase RPC (`fn_validate_and_record_gps_attendance`), where the server calculates geospatial Haversine distance against authorized work location geofences, validates accuracy thresholds, checks shift rules, creates atomic attendance punches with source `MOBILE_GPS`, and writes audit/violation logs.
> - **Bidirectional Realtime Sync**: HR changes to geofences, radiuses, or employee assignments broadcast via Supabase Realtime to Flutter instantly. Mobile punches broadcast live to the HR Web dashboard without any page refresh.

